[b]Tweezer & Kangaroo Zones[/b] detects two specific reversal candlestick patterns — tweezer tops/bottoms and kangaroo tails (pin bars) — and converts them into supply and demand zones that persist over time.

[b]What it does[/b]

Where most candlestick indicators just mark the pattern and move on, this script uses the detected pattern as the origin point for a dynamic zone. Overlapping zones are merged, and zones expire after a set lifetime or a close through them. The result is a living map of supply and demand levels grounded in actual rejection events.

[b]Features[/b]

[list]
[*][b]Pattern detection[/b] — Tweezer tops/bottoms and kangaroo tails with timeframe-sensitive sensitivity settings
[*][b]Zone ranking[/b] — an internal 5-component ranking (rejection, extreme proximity, impulse, freshness, cleanliness) highlights the Top N active zones and dims the rest; it creates no grades and does not affect signals
[*][b]Zone labels[/b] — direction and pattern, with a tooltip showing the raw zone measures and the invalidation level
[*][b]Zone merging[/b] — Overlapping zones are consolidated to reduce clutter
[*][b]Structure context[/b] — HH/HL/LH/LL swing detection for directional bias
[*][b]HTF stack panel[/b] — Up to 3 timeframes displayed in a summary panel
[*][b]Retest signals[/b] — first retest of a zone, optionally only with the higher-timeframe trend on the signal's side
[/list]

[b]Alerts[/b]
All alerts fire only on confirmed bar close by default (configurable via "Alerts only on bar close" toggle).
[list]
[*][b]Buy (zone retest)[/b] — price retests a demand zone for the first time (HTF trend up, if required)
[*][b]Sell (zone retest)[/b] — price retests a supply zone for the first time (HTF trend down, if required)
[/list]

